Z||000004||MontanaFiero||03-25-2001||03:04 AM||||I think the horn fits the car. It may not sound all that big and intimidating, but you aren't driving an 1972 impala! I think you would get some pretty strange looks if you were driving by and in an attempt to honk at one of your buddies and out came this bellowing air-horn sound. Truck (and pickup truck) horns sound like they belong on a truck. "beep-beep" horns sound like they belong on a little car-- exactly what we have.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||filthyscarecrow||03-25-2001||07:30 PM||||just get one of those 135dB italian air horns. that's what i have on mine. my dad honked it once at some guy who was stopped at a green light- just a little tap of the horn- and the junior high schoolers on the corner jumped like they just heard shots ring out. i think a couple of them wet their pants too. it was almost as funny as the time the high school choir teacher slipped and fell on a banana peel. it's very aggressive, very loud and it fits the car pretty well. or you could go with the "dukes of hazzard" horn. that would be a great touch to any fiero (note the sarcasm).<P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
